Q: This keyword initialization in java:
Definition of this keyword in Java
this is a reference variable that refers to the current object of a class.
 Uses of this keyword
1. To refer current class instance variable
Used when local variable and instance variable have same name.

class Demo {
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }

    void show() {
        this.display();  // calling method using this
    }
}

OUTPUT:
Hello
